Andy Johnson wrote:

> I can type either qwerty (my original) or dvorak easily. Dvorak is by 
> FAR easier, though perhaps not faster. When I started playing NetHack I 
> was using a Dvorak, so that's my NetHack layout, even if I'm using 
> qwerty in other applications at the time.
>
> Dvorak is not hard to learn. It only took me a week to type fluently, 
> another week to type quickly, and then about another week before I could 
> switch easily between qwerty and dvorak. This does not mean I couldn't 
> use qwerty for 3 weeks, it just took a while for it to be comfortable. I 
> find my hands get much less tired with Dvorak, but I'll still use qwerty 
